      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9260516::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting atomic mobility favors successful homogeneous alloy formation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10621632::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid or low-temperature processing induces nearly simultaneous reduction of all metal precursors.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid or low-temperature processing restricts free-atom diffusion.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10621632::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed initial material is a homogeneous solid or supported precursor mixture containing near-equimolar noble-metal ions.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen",
        "PMC10873330::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minimizing temperature gradients in an inert or reducing atmosphere limits atomic mobility.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nearly simultaneous reduction produces rapidly formed, uniformly nucleated clusters.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The uniformly nucleated clusters serve as seeds for subsequent alloy growth.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low atomic mobility prevents metal atoms from diffusing and segregating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kinetic trapping promotes a random, single-phase alloy across the multielement system.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10621632::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with slower reduction of the same precursor composition, the modified synthesis will produce a more homogeneous alloy structure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9260516::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with slower reduction, the modified synthesis will reduce elemental segregation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9260516::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC10621632::web::026::simulated_particle_formation_and_influen"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with slower reduction, the modified synthesis will enhance surface-atom exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanism should apply when the metal precursors have similar reduction kinetics and atomic diffusion is effectively inhibited.",
